    not_duplicate_of: []  # dbbe
    pr_ref:  # dbbe
    description: "Surfaced by the WI-huhum adversarial review (workflow wf_497e0e7f-d7b). The WI-huhum scope-boundary walk in py.py::_emit_module_attr_refs fixes over-attribution (a nested read credited to the enclosing function) and the nested-param shadow. Two residual confidently-wrong-RESOLVED-edge cases remain under the WI-huhum references retarget, BOTH pre-existing and SHARED with the sibling _emit_variable_refs (module-level variable reads):\n\n(1c) ENCLOSING-SCOPE closure-capture shadow: with a module-level 'import config as cfg', 'def outer(cfg): def inner(): return cfg.CONFIG' — inner's own pass retargets cfg.CONFIG to the module CONFIG, but cfg is outer's PARAM captured by closure. inner's local_bindings (immediate scope) excludes outer's param, so the guard misses it. Needs the LEGB enclosing-scope binding UNION (the scope-stack machinery already exists: local_names_by_func_id / _build_scope_stack).\n\n(2) MODULE-SCOPE rebind shadow: 'import config as cfg; cfg = make_cfg(); X = cfg.CONFIG' at module scope — the module-scope caller passes EMPTY local_bindings, so a module-level reassignment of the import alias is unguarded. Needs a module-scope shadow set that EXCLUDES plain import aliases (analogous to _collect_local_bindings(include_import_aliases=False); _collect_module_local_names includes imports so cannot be used as-is). The sibling _emit_variable_refs(module_level_nodes, module_symbol) has the identical empty-bindings gap.\n\nBoth are contrived (require a param/local/module-var named identically to a module-level import alias AND a kind=variable target). Recommended structural fix: extract ONE shared scope-bounded walk + enclosing-union shadow helper and route BOTH _emit_module_attr_refs and _emit_variable_refs through it (DRY), closing both helpers' latent gap in one stroke. INV-fahub."  # dbbe
    fields: {}  # dbbe
- op: discuss  # 4f31
  at: '2026-07-14T18:03:17Z'  # 4f31
  by: agent  # 4f31
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4f31
  clock: 2  # 4f31
  nonce: 4f31  # 4f31
  message: "FIXED — described gaps closed (2026-07-14, PR merged to dev @ 3bdba7d51f). The 2 residual INV-fahub confidently-wrong-RESOLVED-edge gaps this item describes — (1c) enclosing-scope closure-capture and (2) module-scope rebind — are closed for BOTH emitters (_emit_module_attr_refs + _emit_variable_refs), for the param / local-assignment / import rebind forms:\n- (1c) enclosing: _enclosing_shadow unions every strict-enclosing function's local_names_by_func_id into the nested scope's shadow set, walking the full chain transitively.\n- (2) module-scope: _collect_module_rebound_names (module-level assignment targets, for the attr retarget) + _collect_module_import_aliases (module-level import aliases, for the variable-ref retarget) passed to the module-scope emit calls.\nAll changes only ADD names to shadow sets, so the effect is bounded to resolved->phantom (a missed retarget), never phantom->resolved or a new wrong edge.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: 6 TDD tests (4 RED->GREEN for the gaps [attr+var x enclosing+module], a transitive 3-level enclosing test, a comprehension-precision test), 100% coverage, full analysis test file green. A 3-lens adversarial review (wf_e116c75e) caught + fixed a comprehension-over-collection regression the fix introduced, a vacuous test, and the missing transitive test.\n\nDOCUMENTED RESIDUALS (advance-not-close, not false-satisfied): the fix handles the assignment/param/import rebind forms this item describes; it does NOT close the PATHOLOGICAL name-collision forms the review surfaced — a def / class / `except E as X` statement name COLLIDING WITH a module import alias keeps its wrong retarget (both module-scope and enclosing; the enclosing case needs a dedicated per-function shadow collector distinct from the LEGB local_names set). Plus INV-fahub-SAFE missed-retarget nits (all phantoms, never wrong edges): the enclosing plain-import over-approximation, enclosing global/nonlocal declarations, and flow-insensitive reassignment ordering. Recommend leaving open (todo_soft) for the pathological name-collision residual, or filing a focused follow-up; the item's originally-described gaps are closed with evidence."  # 4f31
