- op: discuss  # 6dea
  at: '2026-07-29T01:37:15Z'  # 6dea
  by: agent  # 6dea
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6dea
  clock: 6  # 6dea
  nonce: 6dea  # 6dea
  message: "DONE — PR #59 merged, dev @ b8ada2f2eb (CI green; 2374 passed, all changed sources 100% cov).\n\nThe item's ORIGINALLY-described gaps (1c enclosing closure-capture, 2 module-scope rebind) were already closed 2026-07-14. This closes the RESIDUAL it was kept open for: the pathological statement-name-collides-with-import-alias family.\n\nREPRODUCED FIRST (all four, live, before any code changed) — each a confidently-wrong RESOLVED edge to the module's real first-party symbol, i.e. the INV-fahub failure class:\n  - module-level 'def cfg' shadowing 'import pkg.config as cfg'\n  - module-level 'class cfg'\n  - 'except ValueError as cfg'\n  - an ENCLOSING function's nested 'def cfg', read from an inner function\nPlus a fifth form the in-code note listed and I folded in: a walrus '(cfg := y)' inside a comprehension, which per PEP 572 binds in the CONTAINING scope.\n\nROOT CAUSE: the shadow sets were built from ast.Name/ast.Store assignment targets. All five forms bind a name WITHOUT a Store target — def/class bind via the statement, ExceptHandler.name is a bare str, and the walrus leaks out of a scope the Store-walk deliberately skips.\n\nFIX: new _collect_statement_binding_names, unioned into (a) _collect_module_rebound_names for module scope and (b) _enclosing_shadow via a per-function map built inside _extract_edges — which already has the tree and func_symbol_by_node_id, so NO FileAnalysis field was threaded. Kept deliberately SEPARATE from _collect_scope_local_names, exactly as the item's residual note prescribed: that set feeds the LEGB lookup, which resolves def/class names to their NestedDef bindings directly and would break if they became opaque locals. Shadow set != lookup set.\n\nSAFETY (structural, not incidental): every name added can only turn a retarget resolved -> phantom (a missed retarget), never phantom -> resolved. The suppressed shape falls back to the generic module_attr_ref against the synthetic 0-0 attribute stand-in — the pre-retarget baseline.\n\nTESTS: 6 new (4 pathological forms + walrus + a NON-VACUOUS control asserting an unshadowed alias STILL retargets to the real CONFIG variable, so the shadow cannot silently over-approximate). py.py at 100%.\n\nTWO MEASUREMENT LESSONS worth recording (both bit me, both self-caught):\n  (1) My first analyzer-level probe used 'from pkg import config as cfg' and produced NO retarget even for the CONTROL — the fixture, not the code, was wrong; the retarget gate keys on module_imports, which the plain 'import pkg.config as cfg' form populates. Establish a positive control before concluding anything from a null result.\n  (2) My first verdict after the fix read '** WRONG **' on all four because the probe matched 'CONFIG' as a SUBSTRING of the dst — which matches both the real node and the suppressed phantom. The fix had worked the whole time. Check is_resolved and the exact dst, not a substring.\n  (3) The first draft of the pytest assertions ('no edge anywhere targets CONFIG') failed on the containment linker's entirely correct 'contains' file->variable edge. Scope such an assertion to the retarget edge types AND the reading file.\n\nRESIDUAL: none for this item — all five forms the in-code notes listed are now collected, and both in-code residual notes (in _collect_module_rebound_names and _enclosing_shadow) were rewritten from 'documented residual' to the implemented contract."  # 6dea
